{title: Forged from Bronze and Iron}
{subtitle: Genesis 4:22; 4:17–24; 4:23–24; 4:20–22}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 80}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Zillah gave birth to a new son
Cain was building his first city
Lamech took two wives for his own
One named Adah, the other Zillah
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Adah bore Jabal the nomad
Father of those with tents and flocks
Jubal played the lyre and pipe
[C]Father of all who hear the song [Dm]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Tu-bal-Cain forged the metal tools
Out of [G]bronze and iron bright
[Dm]He shaped the hammer and the tongs
Under [C]the heavy weight of [Dm]night
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
His sister Naamah stood beside
Name recorded in the old genealogy
Jabal lived among the tents
[C]Jubal played the ancient melodies [Dm]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [G] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [C] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Lamech sang to Adah and Zillah
Hear my voice and listen close
I killed a man for wounding me
A [C]young man for his slight abuse [Dm]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
If Cain is avenged seven times
La[G]mech sev-en-ty-sev-[Dm]en times
Forged from bronze and iron
[C]In the lineage of [Dm]Cain
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [G] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [C] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | ×2
